  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B053",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B010",
    "B003"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration has changed from B010 to B053. IceCube remains a profound observational opening, but the unresolved question of how two people can fairly represent the decisive work of a large collaboration is consequential at the final-vote stage. Optical lattice clocks instead combine a distinct physical advance, exceptional experimental maturity, independent reproducibility, and a notably clean two-person allocation. Katori and Ye represent complementary, decisive leadership in making neutral-atom lattice clocks a stable precision-measurement platform. The achievement has enduring basic-physics significance while also providing an experimental capability whose value does not depend on promised future applications.",
    "case_against": "The broadest consequences of optical lattice clocks, including standard-setting and some fundamental-physics tests, are still developing. The citation should therefore reward the development of the clocks themselves, not claim achievements that remain prospective. B010 retains a stronger claim to opening an entirely new astronomical messenger channel, while B003 is exceptionally mature and cleanly delimited.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson identifies optical lattice clocks as a mature, reproducible achievement with unusually clear complementary credit for Katori and Ye, while noting that their ultimate standard-setting role is still developing.",
        "response": "I agree with that balance. The developing standard-setting role is a reason to keep the citation narrow, not to discount a measurement capability that is already mature, independently reproduced, and physically distinctive. The clarity of the Katori-Ye allocation is especially important when several otherwise powerful proposals have unresolved historical boundaries."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson argues that inflation transformed cosmology and connects early-universe physics to observed primordial structure, but recognizes the unresolved role of Linde and the fact that observations do not uniquely select inflation.",
        "response": "I agree that B023 is one of the most intellectually consequential subjects before us. At this stage, however, its attribution problem and the distinction between support for a broad framework and unique empirical confirmation make a final three-person configuration less secure. B053 offers a more exact match among achievement, maturity, citation, and credited individuals."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth argues that the recollision model and quantum theory of high-harmonic generation are a coherent, experimentally validated foundation, provided they are kept separate from the wider attosecond experimental revolution.",
        "response": "I accept the strength and maturity of B020, particularly its clear mechanism-to-experiment trajectory. Her qualification is decisive, however: the necessary boundary from already recognized attosecond experimental advances remains delicate. B053 can be stated and credited without an equivalent risk of overlapping a broader previously recognized enterprise."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record confirms that Katori and Ye alone adequately represent the decisive development of optical lattice clocks.",
      "How far the citation may refer to precision measurement without improperly claiming future standard-setting or fundamental-physics outcomes."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
